WEBVTT

00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:16.490
Polar Bear's Café

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:34.940
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:01:30.910 --> 00:01:34.030
Panda's New Part-time Job!

00:01:39.080 --> 00:01:40.870
Hello!

00:01:43.030 --> 00:01:45.330
What's with the getup?

00:01:48.030 --> 00:01:51.340
I'm starting a new job that 
I'll be doing once a week.

00:01:51.340 --> 00:01:52.630
What?!

00:01:52.630 --> 00:01:54.510
You're not quitting but 
adding another job?

00:01:55.520 --> 00:01:56.970
Yup.

00:01:59.380 --> 00:02:01.640
That's a very cute panda design.

00:02:03.610 --> 00:02:06.500
You get it, too, Miss Sasako?

00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:08.910
So, what kind of job is it?

00:02:08.910 --> 00:02:10.230
A roller!

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:11.880
Roller?

00:02:12.820 --> 00:02:14.690
I have no idea what 
you're talking about.

00:02:15.470 --> 00:02:17.270
You don't know what that is?

00:02:17.270 --> 00:02:19.700
A roller. Rol-ler.

00:02:22.810 --> 00:02:25.120
Curlers. We did that 
before, didn't we?

00:02:25.770 --> 00:02:27.870
Sailor. We did that, too.

00:02:28.350 --> 00:02:30.080
Dealer. Yep, that, too.

00:02:30.380 --> 00:02:32.360
Oh, that's it!

00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:33.180
What?

00:02:33.640 --> 00:02:36.570
Not a roller, I meant a dealer.

00:02:36.570 --> 00:02:38.210
You're going to work at a casino?

00:02:38.830 --> 00:02:42.580
Nope. I'm going to sell 
cool-looking cars.

00:02:42.580 --> 00:02:45.220
You mean at a car dealership?

00:02:45.220 --> 00:02:48.060
You? You're going to sell cars?

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:51.980
I'll be fine. I'm wearing a tie.

00:02:54.060 --> 00:02:56.440
Why on earth would they hire you?

00:02:57.130 --> 00:03:00.110
Oh, I'm so excited.

00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:03.040
I wonder what I'll have to do.

00:03:04.610 --> 00:03:06.150
I think that you might be selling,

00:03:06.150 --> 00:03:07.410
you know... cars.

00:03:07.410 --> 00:03:11.420
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:30.330
Oh?

00:03:31.330 --> 00:03:33.100
Are you a customer?

00:03:34.120 --> 00:03:35.460
I am...

00:03:37.460 --> 00:03:39.250
Welcome!

00:03:40.480 --> 00:03:42.200
And you are?

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:44.720
I'm Panda, the new hire.

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:46.510
Oh, I see.

00:03:46.510 --> 00:03:48.780
Then could you help me out a little?

00:03:48.780 --> 00:03:50.950
Only if it's a little.

00:03:54.160 --> 00:03:55.700
What is it?

00:03:55.700 --> 00:03:59.670
So, what options do you 
have for this car?

00:04:00.460 --> 00:04:02.130
What's an option?

00:04:05.410 --> 00:04:06.550
So...

00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:09.310
Does this have airbags?

00:04:10.020 --> 00:04:11.730
It'll go back.

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:13.230
Would you like it to go back?

00:04:13.480 --> 00:04:14.290
Huh?

00:04:15.530 --> 00:04:16.690
How's the gas mileage?

00:04:17.420 --> 00:04:20.150
Don't you have any other questions?

00:04:21.650 --> 00:04:24.110
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:04:25.480 --> 00:04:26.540
Like what?

00:04:27.130 --> 00:04:30.610
Like about pandas or bamboo?

00:04:31.640 --> 00:04:34.120
Is there someone else I can talk to?

00:04:34.490 --> 00:04:36.630
Which would you like to ask about?

00:04:36.630 --> 00:04:37.330
What?

00:04:38.160 --> 00:04:40.550
Which would you like to ask about?

00:04:42.290 --> 00:04:44.010
Pandas, I guess?

00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:51.970
Pandas look like this!

00:04:53.970 --> 00:04:59.190
You're cute and all, 
but I'm a bit lost here...

00:04:59.190 --> 00:05:01.650
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:05:02.330 --> 00:05:04.360
What a patient customer...

00:05:05.320 --> 00:05:08.120
Being natural is very 
important, isn't it?

00:05:08.600 --> 00:05:12.840
I think that only works at the zoo.

00:05:12.840 --> 00:05:14.880
But I was able to sell a car, too.

00:05:15.440 --> 00:05:17.410
What?! How?

00:05:17.960 --> 00:05:20.590
I told you, I was being natural.

00:05:20.590 --> 00:05:27.550
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:05:31.400 --> 00:05:33.920
I can't believe he still 
hasn't woken up.

00:05:40.020 --> 00:05:42.270
Why's there a panda on the car?

00:05:42.270 --> 00:05:43.190
Huh?

00:05:44.420 --> 00:05:46.480
Th-The body's so strong,

00:05:46.480 --> 00:05:49.870
even a panda can lay on 
it without denting it!

00:05:49.870 --> 00:05:52.130
And our state-of-the-art 
engine is so much quieter

00:05:52.130 --> 00:05:55.700
than our competitors, it's not 
even disturbing his sleep.

00:06:01.950 --> 00:06:04.150
He seems really comfortable.

00:06:04.150 --> 00:06:05.390
I know...

00:06:07.370 --> 00:06:09.350
Could I take it for a test drive?

00:06:09.890 --> 00:06:11.430
Thank you very much!

00:06:12.360 --> 00:06:14.100
That would be the salesman's sale.

00:06:14.840 --> 00:06:18.510
But he said it was because of me.

00:06:19.040 --> 00:06:21.430
He said sales have gone up,

00:06:21.430 --> 00:06:24.020
and asked me to sleep 
on top of cars again.

00:06:24.450 --> 00:06:26.500
So you're more of a mascot

00:06:26.500 --> 00:06:27.990
than a salesman.

00:06:28.420 --> 00:06:31.570
Anyway, I'm glad things are 
going well for you.

00:06:31.570 --> 00:06:34.020
So I changed jobs.

00:06:34.020 --> 00:06:35.160
Why?!

00:06:36.050 --> 00:06:39.500
One of our regulars is the 
head of his own company,

00:06:40.060 --> 00:06:43.250
and I got asked to work there.

00:06:43.760 --> 00:06:46.040
What kind of job is it?

00:06:46.760 --> 00:06:49.970
It's like "sell, sell, buy, buy" 
<i>(uri, uri, kai, kai)</i>.

00:06:49.970 --> 00:06:51.180
Melon, melon <i>(uri, uri)</i>?

00:06:51.180 --> 00:07:01.190
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:07:01.190 --> 00:07:03.150
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:07:01.360 --> 00:07:02.660
Shell, shell <i>(kai, kai)</i>?

00:07:07.660 --> 00:07:10.720
You were exactly correct in regards 
to Marubi's stocks, sir.

00:07:11.260 --> 00:07:13.760
I see. What's going 
on with Yotsubishi?

00:07:14.830 --> 00:07:20.000
Dept. Chief

00:07:16.260 --> 00:07:18.820
Since when is a panda 
the department chief?

00:07:19.320 --> 00:07:20.000
What?

00:07:20.660 --> 00:07:25.210
Um, what does this company do?

00:07:25.690 --> 00:07:29.010
It looks like he's not actually 
the department chief.

00:07:29.510 --> 00:07:30.420
Are you lost?

00:07:31.070 --> 00:07:33.090
I'm a new employee.

00:07:33.450 --> 00:07:35.320
A new employee?

00:07:35.320 --> 00:07:38.600
Looks like HR is getting creative...

00:07:39.270 --> 00:07:42.060
What does sell, sell, 
buy, buy mean?

00:07:42.350 --> 00:07:46.340
Why don't you look 
after him for a while?

00:07:46.340 --> 00:07:48.150
What?! Me?

00:07:48.150 --> 00:07:54.160
Polar Bear's Café

00:07:54.690 --> 00:07:55.730
All right.

00:07:55.730 --> 00:07:58.370
I'll explain it one more time, 
so listen carefully.

00:07:58.760 --> 00:08:01.330
This is called a support line,

00:08:01.330 --> 00:08:03.570
and if it goes under 
this line, you sell.

00:08:03.570 --> 00:08:06.250
If it gets closer to 
the line, you buy.

00:08:06.800 --> 00:08:10.340
And when this thin 
line connects here...

00:08:12.140 --> 00:08:13.300
He's asleep?!

00:08:17.120 --> 00:08:19.260
He's cute and all, but...

00:08:19.260 --> 00:08:21.770
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:08:27.020 --> 00:08:29.420
Sell... sell...

00:08:30.150 --> 00:08:33.190
buy... bamboo grass...

00:08:33.190 --> 00:08:35.780
Could I get a large serving 
of bamboo grass?

00:08:37.760 --> 00:08:39.350
And you bought 100,000 shares

00:08:39.350 --> 00:08:41.160
with the company's money?!

00:08:41.600 --> 00:08:42.510
Yup.

00:08:43.270 --> 00:08:45.620
Why on earth would they hire you?

00:08:46.090 --> 00:08:49.590
But apparently, they 
made a lot of money.

00:08:49.590 --> 00:08:52.130
Really?! How?

00:08:53.800 --> 00:08:55.090
Coincidentally?

00:08:55.570 --> 00:08:57.580
You have very good luck, Panda.

00:08:58.160 --> 00:08:59.570
But you know,

00:08:59.570 --> 00:09:02.500
you're not going to be able to 
keep the job with just luck.

00:09:02.500 --> 00:09:05.930
Maybe you should quit 
while you're ahead.

00:09:05.930 --> 00:09:07.230
I did.

00:09:07.230 --> 00:09:08.940
You did?!

00:09:08.940 --> 00:09:10.690
You changed jobs again?

00:09:10.690 --> 00:09:11.820
Yup.

00:09:11.820 --> 00:09:15.380
Now I'm going to be a lecturer 
at a sales seminar.

00:09:15.380 --> 00:09:16.350
What?!

00:09:16.950 --> 00:09:19.450
What are you going to be 
able to teach exactly?

00:09:19.450 --> 00:09:20.820
By the way,

00:09:22.340 --> 00:09:24.330
what's that decorative plant

00:09:24.330 --> 00:09:26.860
in the doorway?

00:09:26.860 --> 00:09:27.720
You're going with that?

00:09:27.720 --> 00:09:30.260
How about the guy standing 
next to the plant?

00:09:30.260 --> 00:09:31.520
Who is that?

00:09:31.520 --> 00:09:32.910
He's my secretary.

00:09:32.910 --> 00:09:33.420
What?!

00:09:33.420 --> 00:09:35.380
Panda's Secretary
Maruyama

00:09:33.850 --> 00:09:35.380
My name is Maruyama.

00:09:35.830 --> 00:09:37.510
Oh, thank you.

00:09:37.510 --> 00:09:38.840
My name is Penguin.

00:09:39.250 --> 00:09:42.520
Could you get him some bamboo 
grass, too, Polar Bear?

00:09:42.520 --> 00:09:43.810
A large serving, please.

00:09:44.290 --> 00:09:46.560
I think he'd prefer coffee.

00:09:46.560 --> 00:09:49.520
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:09:49.520 --> 00:09:54.280
Living Candidly
Marketing and the Power of Communication

00:09:52.350 --> 00:09:55.530
Hello, I'm Panda.

00:09:56.470 --> 00:09:59.500
What I want to talk about today

00:09:59.500 --> 00:10:02.320
is how to live life.

00:10:04.120 --> 00:10:08.830
I work twice a week at the zoo.

00:10:09.770 --> 00:10:12.210
This is a picture of that.

00:10:13.150 --> 00:10:16.480
The person lazing around 
with me is my mentor,

00:10:16.480 --> 00:10:18.180
Mr. Full-time Panda.

00:10:19.270 --> 00:10:23.000
Please take a look at 
page two of your handout.

00:10:23.000 --> 00:10:26.090
There is a very important 
picture there.

00:10:29.570 --> 00:10:33.500
That is me getting sucked up
by my mom's vacuum.

00:10:34.440 --> 00:10:36.700
What's the point of this lecture?

00:10:36.700 --> 00:10:37.920
No idea.

00:10:37.920 --> 00:10:39.820
But he is cute.

00:10:40.520 --> 00:10:42.280
Next...

00:10:46.640 --> 00:10:48.960
Man, he was so cute!

00:10:48.960 --> 00:10:51.300
This was a nice change of pace.

00:10:52.060 --> 00:10:53.960
Let's do our best starting tomorrow.

00:10:53.960 --> 00:10:57.460
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:10:57.930 --> 00:10:58.990
I see.

00:10:58.990 --> 00:11:00.870
So the workplace morale went up

00:11:00.870 --> 00:11:02.360
and performance improved.

00:11:02.360 --> 00:11:03.820
Oh, I see.

00:11:04.350 --> 00:11:05.110
Yup.

00:11:05.110 --> 00:11:08.410
Really?! Is the world 
really that simple?!

00:11:08.410 --> 00:11:10.750
I even released a book.

00:11:10.750 --> 00:11:11.370
A book?

00:11:11.810 --> 00:11:12.930
This would be it, sir.

00:11:13.690 --> 00:11:15.320
Living Candidly

00:11:13.690 --> 00:11:15.320
Panda

00:11:13.690 --> 00:11:15.320
Highly Praised in the Business World!!

00:11:16.440 --> 00:11:18.210
I included my autograph.

00:11:19.900 --> 00:11:23.070
Wow. So you released a photobook?

00:11:23.070 --> 00:11:24.760
It's a business guide.

00:11:25.260 --> 00:11:28.020
No matter how you look at it,
this is just a photobook.

00:11:28.020 --> 00:11:30.620
Then a lot of other things 
happened and now...

00:11:30.620 --> 00:11:32.580
Panda

00:11:34.770 --> 00:11:36.590
CEO?

00:11:36.990 --> 00:11:37.700
Yes.

00:11:37.700 --> 00:11:39.420
He is the CEO.

00:11:40.030 --> 00:11:43.010
I wonder what CEO means.

00:11:43.010 --> 00:11:44.280
Calculating

00:11:44.280 --> 00:11:45.380
Egotistical

00:11:47.200 --> 00:11:48.270
Your turn, Miss Sasako.

00:11:49.220 --> 00:11:50.680
Opportune moments?

00:11:52.340 --> 00:11:55.820
Well, I guess that's one 
way of explaining it,

00:11:55.820 --> 00:11:59.350
but CEO stands for Chief 
Executive Officer, doesn't it?

00:11:59.350 --> 00:12:01.650
They're the most important 
person in a company.

00:12:02.210 --> 00:12:04.980
So I'm not just cute,

00:12:04.980 --> 00:12:06.450
I'm important.

00:12:06.450 --> 00:12:08.750
That's impressive, Panda.

00:12:08.750 --> 00:12:11.660
Should we be ending this 
conversation with "impressive"?

00:12:12.210 --> 00:12:14.120
Pardon my interruption,

00:12:14.610 --> 00:12:17.890
but we should be leaving 
soon, Mr. Panda.

00:12:25.060 --> 00:12:26.510
See you later!

00:12:35.840 --> 00:12:39.870
Life is filled with an endless 
amount of opportunities.

00:12:39.870 --> 00:12:41.880
No, this can't be right.

00:12:41.880 --> 00:12:43.170
It can't?

00:12:43.170 --> 00:12:44.240
No, it can't.

00:12:44.240 --> 00:12:53.250
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:12:53.870 --> 00:12:55.710
Hello.

00:12:56.120 --> 00:12:57.380
Welcome.

00:12:57.380 --> 00:12:59.600
Oh? Where's your necktie?

00:12:59.600 --> 00:13:01.170
Are you off from work today?

00:13:01.800 --> 00:13:04.680
I was told I didn't 
need to come anymore.

00:13:05.000 --> 00:13:07.810
I see. I'm sorry to hear that.

00:13:07.810 --> 00:13:10.850
Or rather, I'm surprised 
you lasted that long.

00:13:11.840 --> 00:13:15.850
Oh? Mr. Penguin's not here today?

00:13:16.590 --> 00:13:19.060
Hey! Why are you sleeping?

00:13:19.650 --> 00:13:22.030
Huh? Well...

00:13:23.110 --> 00:13:26.650
I thought I could become 
a CEO if I laid here...

00:13:27.950 --> 00:13:32.910
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:13:29.430 --> 00:13:31.780
Mr. Penguin Goes Flying!

00:13:38.520 --> 00:13:40.390
What a nice day.

00:13:47.420 --> 00:13:49.650
That looks so relaxing.

00:13:50.920 --> 00:13:52.090
You know,

00:13:52.750 --> 00:13:54.730
my scalp is actually black.

00:13:57.130 --> 00:13:59.530
Though you probably 
couldn't tell because

00:13:59.530 --> 00:14:01.570
I'm covered in white fur.

00:14:01.570 --> 00:14:03.150
No, we can't.

00:14:03.770 --> 00:14:05.530
Should I shave somewhere?

00:14:05.860 --> 00:14:06.950
That's all right.

00:14:07.330 --> 00:14:08.430
Oh.

00:14:09.300 --> 00:14:11.360
I want to be able to fly.

00:14:13.120 --> 00:14:13.910
Hm?

00:14:14.630 --> 00:14:16.250
Do you want another drink?

00:14:16.250 --> 00:14:17.880
Completely ignoring that, huh?

00:14:18.360 --> 00:14:20.880
You don't really need to fly.

00:14:20.880 --> 00:14:22.840
That was a fast rejection.

00:14:23.470 --> 00:14:25.800
It would be nice to be able to fly.

00:14:26.160 --> 00:14:28.260
So you get what I'm 
saying, Miss Sasako?

00:14:28.870 --> 00:14:31.180
I'd be able to easily get 
from my house to the café.

00:14:33.510 --> 00:14:35.220
That's not what I mean.

00:14:36.680 --> 00:14:38.140
What do you mean?

00:14:38.450 --> 00:14:39.870
How do I say this...

00:14:39.870 --> 00:14:42.830
Like when you swim in the 
ocean, it's really fun.

00:14:43.230 --> 00:14:46.720
But I think it'd be 
amazing to fly, too.

00:14:54.410 --> 00:14:56.800
You can't fly at all, huh?

00:14:56.800 --> 00:14:59.010
I already told you that.

00:14:59.010 --> 00:15:00.590
But you have wings.

00:15:00.590 --> 00:15:02.000
These aren't wings.

00:15:02.550 --> 00:15:03.750
They're flippers <i>(furippa)</i>.

00:15:05.340 --> 00:15:06.460
Those would be slippers <i>(surippa)</i>!

00:15:07.190 --> 00:15:08.420
That would be a kappa!

00:15:08.940 --> 00:15:10.430
That would be a rapper <i>(rappa)</i>!

00:15:09.090 --> 00:15:10.430
Hey ma—

00:15:11.080 --> 00:15:14.320
Flippers are like fins, right?

00:15:15.000 --> 00:15:17.090
So they're not wings?

00:15:17.880 --> 00:15:20.440
How are you supposed to fly, then?

00:15:22.630 --> 00:15:23.520
With conviction?

00:15:24.090 --> 00:15:27.570
If that's all it took, 
I think everyone could fly.

00:15:28.350 --> 00:15:31.000
I have a good idea.

00:15:33.880 --> 00:15:36.000
All right, Mr. Penguin!

00:15:36.440 --> 00:15:38.070
Try taking flight!

00:15:38.750 --> 00:15:40.870
There's no way I could fly like this.

00:15:41.280 --> 00:15:42.410
Mr. Penguin.

00:15:43.960 --> 00:15:45.810
Over here, over here.

00:15:51.770 --> 00:15:54.850
I didn't put these on to 
start a fire for you guys.

00:15:55.520 --> 00:15:57.410
Isn't there any other way?

00:15:58.190 --> 00:16:00.310
What? How about...

00:16:03.860 --> 00:16:06.790
I guess there's no point in just 
sticking feathers on you.

00:16:07.290 --> 00:16:09.280
Realize that before you do it!

00:16:11.760 --> 00:16:13.870
Now you're going to 
stick a balloon on me?

00:16:19.950 --> 00:16:21.250
Wow!

00:16:21.600 --> 00:16:23.540
You've lost the point!

00:16:26.020 --> 00:16:28.200
What are you trying to accomplish

00:16:28.200 --> 00:16:30.000
by sticking a fan on my back?

00:16:30.630 --> 00:16:31.640
Propellers?

00:16:32.330 --> 00:16:34.480
I think this plan is going to fail,

00:16:34.480 --> 00:16:35.510
but how are we going to turn it on?

00:16:36.900 --> 00:16:38.330
We'll use an extension cord.

00:16:39.730 --> 00:16:42.240
That won't reach the sky!

00:16:42.240 --> 00:16:44.900
No, you wouldn't be able 
to fly with this.

00:16:47.200 --> 00:16:48.320
What about fireworks?

00:16:49.910 --> 00:16:52.410
I don't see that ending well for me.

00:16:54.610 --> 00:16:56.520
He's complaining a lot.

00:16:56.520 --> 00:16:59.950
We're not birds, so it's 
not like we'd know.

00:17:00.500 --> 00:17:02.930
What do you have to do to fly?

00:17:02.930 --> 00:17:04.930
You're asking <i>me</i> that?

00:17:05.800 --> 00:17:07.270
Hold on one sec...

00:17:11.330 --> 00:17:13.790
What do you think, 
Mr. Crested Serpent Eagle?

00:17:13.790 --> 00:17:16.170
Why did you call me out 
here all of a sudden?

00:17:16.170 --> 00:17:20.180
Mr. Penguin says he wants 
to fly, no matter what.

00:17:20.180 --> 00:17:21.690
Oh.

00:17:22.080 --> 00:17:23.830
Well, here we go.

00:17:26.150 --> 00:17:27.970
Ow, ow, ow, ow!

00:17:27.970 --> 00:17:29.930
Ow! Ow, ow, ow!

00:17:29.930 --> 00:17:31.760
Hey! He's flying.

00:17:31.760 --> 00:17:33.360
Good, he's flying.

00:17:33.720 --> 00:17:35.660
Congratulations.

00:17:37.860 --> 00:17:38.740
Is that enough?

00:17:39.240 --> 00:17:40.740
That's enough!

00:17:42.650 --> 00:17:44.120
Later!

00:17:44.120 --> 00:17:45.870
Thanks!

00:17:49.880 --> 00:17:52.130
See? You're flying.

00:17:52.620 --> 00:17:55.820
I don't feel like I flew at all.

00:17:55.820 --> 00:17:58.590
I only remember pain.

00:17:59.350 --> 00:18:02.380
But your dream came true, Mr. Penguin.

00:18:02.970 --> 00:18:05.220
It's done. It's done.

00:18:05.220 --> 00:18:08.060
But I don't feel like I 
accomplished anything.

00:18:08.790 --> 00:18:11.300
See? A roasted sweet potato.

00:18:11.810 --> 00:18:13.430
Oh, that.

00:18:14.550 --> 00:18:17.680
It's always better when 
you make it in a bonfire.

00:18:17.680 --> 00:18:19.450
It's so warm.

00:18:20.480 --> 00:18:21.830
It's delicious,

00:18:21.830 --> 00:18:24.450
but what happened to 
me trying to fly?

00:18:25.010 --> 00:18:27.770
Mr. Penguin, I thought of something.

00:18:28.960 --> 00:18:31.030
Close your eyes.

00:18:33.050 --> 00:18:37.070
Enjoy flying in the 
world of imagination.

00:18:37.800 --> 00:18:39.020
I decline.

00:18:40.170 --> 00:18:41.050
Hey.

00:18:41.940 --> 00:18:44.020
Oh, Mr. Grizzly.

00:18:44.620 --> 00:18:48.060
Do you know of a good way 
of making Mr. Penguin fly?

00:18:48.570 --> 00:18:49.470
Oh?

00:18:50.090 --> 00:18:52.020
That's easy.

00:18:53.950 --> 00:18:54.940
Up you go!

00:19:02.720 --> 00:19:04.870
That's not what I meant.

00:19:05.220 --> 00:19:06.560
My bad.

00:19:12.980 --> 00:19:16.190
It really does look relaxing.

00:19:28.610 --> 00:19:29.890
Hey,

00:19:30.510 --> 00:19:32.560
I've got a great idea.

00:20:15.270 --> 00:20:16.310
Up we go.

00:20:39.140 --> 00:20:43.300
<i>So this is what a bird sees.</i>

00:20:45.730 --> 00:20:50.770
<i>It's sort of similar to 
being in the ocean.</i>

00:21:08.740 --> 00:21:10.330
Thanks for all of your hard work!

00:21:10.330 --> 00:21:11.980
Thank you for all of your hard work.

00:21:15.550 --> 00:21:17.420
That hits the spot.

00:21:18.180 --> 00:21:20.040
I'm tired.

00:21:20.040 --> 00:21:23.120
I'm happy for Mr. Penguin.

00:21:23.120 --> 00:21:26.100
I didn't know how it was going 
to turn out at one point.

00:21:26.100 --> 00:21:27.430
No kidding.

00:21:34.030 --> 00:21:35.730
Hey!

00:21:37.730 --> 00:21:39.330
Hey!

00:21:40.640 --> 00:21:42.320
Hey!

00:21:44.510 --> 00:21:46.860
I'd like to come down now.

00:21:47.620 --> 00:21:49.490
Hello?

00:21:51.880 --> 00:21:54.650
Pardon... me...

00:21:54.650 --> 00:21:56.870
Huh? What? What?

00:21:58.170 --> 00:22:01.840
Over... here...

00:22:01.840 --> 00:22:04.960
Wait there...

00:22:06.780 --> 00:22:14.350
I'll... come... help... you...

00:22:18.830 --> 00:22:20.400
I wonder

00:22:20.400 --> 00:22:23.260
when I'll be able to get down.

00:23:54.950 --> 00:24:24.790
Next Time

00:23:58.170 --> 00:23:59.580
Mr. Penguin, Mr. Penguin.

00:23:59.580 --> 00:24:00.790
What is it, Panda?

00:24:00.790 --> 00:24:02.940
I'm curious as to why rich old men

00:24:02.940 --> 00:24:05.570
won't make me an heir 
to their fortune.

00:24:05.570 --> 00:24:07.660
That'd be because they 
have no relation to you.

00:24:07.660 --> 00:24:08.930
Then, Mr. Penguin,

00:24:08.930 --> 00:24:10.800
you should send me money each month.

00:24:10.800 --> 00:24:12.030
I immediately decline.

00:24:12.030 --> 00:24:14.340
You're so selfish, Mr. Penguin.

00:24:14.340 --> 00:24:17.040
Apparently the definition for 
"selfish" has been changed.

00:24:17.040 --> 00:24:18.600
Let's end this, Polar Bear.

00:24:18.830 --> 00:24:20.230
Next week's Polar Bear's Café

00:24:20.230 --> 00:24:21.930
will be presented to you in mosaic.

00:24:20.580 --> 00:24:24.640
Halloween
Llama Day

00:24:21.930 --> 00:24:22.970
It will be presented normally.

00:24:22.970 --> 00:24:24.370
Enjoy!
